        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 80-year-old female admitted on 01/12/2017 with an acute exacerbation of her known Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD). On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray and arterial blood gas analysis were performed confirming exacerbation without pneumonic consolidation. Spirometry confirmed severely reduced airflow. She was treated with nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), a course of systemic corticosteroids (prednisolone), and supplemental oxygen therapy. She responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. She was discharged on 02/12/2017 in stable condition. Discharge medications include inhaled bronchodilators and a tapering oral steroid course. Please arrange early follow-up and review of her long-term COPD management plan. Do not hesitate to contact me with any queries.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
